map_board_partition :: proc(b: ^Map_Board, allocator := context.allocator) {
	b.district_tiles = make([dynamic][dynamic]u32, len(b.districts), len(b.districts), allocator)
	for k in 0..<len(b.candidates) {
		d := map_district_assign(b, b.candidates[k])
		append(&b.district_tiles[d], u32(k))
	}
}
The outer array uses `allocator`, but the inner lists grow via bare `append`, which (Odin core_builtin _reserve_dynamic_array_unsafe:1403-1406: `if a.allocator.procedure == nil { a.allocator = context.allocator }`) binds a make-zeroed inner array's stored allocator to context.allocator — not the parameter. Two tests pass a scoped arena expecting full placement (map_test.odin:683): map_board_partition(&b, context.temp_allocator)

